{
  "_doc": "POC content plan for the sgs/nav-drawer variant exit gate (Spec 36 FR-36-6 Task 5). Consumed by build-poc-fixtures.py. Every label and every line of copy here was HARVESTED LIVE from the reference site's open drawer on 2026-07-29 and is recorded in labels-<site>.json in .claude/reports/2026-07-28-drawer-code-extraction/. Nothing here is invented: the design gate's §6 rule is that POC fixtures are exact clones INCLUDING content, so a visual difference between our variant and the reference is attributable to the BLOCK, never to content drift. Genericising this copy is a named PRE-PRODUCTION step (P-DRAWER-VARIANT-CONTENT-GENERICISE), never a POC step.",
  "_navMenuAttrs_note": "Authoring block markup directly does NOT apply a registerBlockVariation's seeded child attributes — those only fire when an operator inserts the variation from the inserter. So each variant's nav-menu attrs are restated here to match variations.js exactly (verified against that file 2026-07-29).",
  "_known_fidelity_limits": [
    "sgs/social-icons has no Vimeo or Dribbble platform slug (render.php $platform_icons). buck uses Vimeo, dogstudio uses Dribbble — both mapped to platform 'website' with a label override. This is a real framework gap vs the references, recorded not hidden.",
    "dogstudio's decorative index numbers (01-05) beside each link are out of scope by the design gate's own out-of-scope list.",
    "lamalama's 'What we do' has a collapsed submenu (Branding/Websites/E-commerce/Marketing) at height:0 — excluded, as it is not part of the default open state.",
    "Two harvested values are dynamic, not fixed strings (studionamma's live city+clock, lamalama's rotating tagline); the mechanism was recorded in the harvest and a stable snapshot is used here."
  ],
